WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.200
I'd call

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.800
the public hearing

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.000
to order.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:08.960
And

00:00:12.415 --> 00:00:15.535
first off, I'd like like to welcome Anne Marie

00:00:15.855 --> 00:00:16.495
to

00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:19.855
the Commission and for joining us. And

00:00:21.695 --> 00:00:23.935
the first section will be a public hearing.

00:00:24.175 --> 00:00:24.735
And

00:00:25.295 --> 00:00:27.055
any of the Commission members

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.140
are able to ask questions as we go through the topics during

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:36.660
the public hearing. Once we actually get to the regular meeting and start deliberation,

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.180
only those

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.860
commission members that

00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:44.705
are actually seated, the five commission members, will be able to

00:00:45.025 --> 00:00:51.985
deliberate on the different articles. So feel free to ask away as we're going through this. Most

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.585
of the articles that

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:59.160
we're talking about we've been working on for quite a while, so I know you're at a little bit of a disadvantage there.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.480
But we'll try and explain

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.360
what they're about as we go through.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.960
I'm looking to see

00:01:10.075 --> 00:01:14.155
if we had anybody from the public join us tonight. And so far,

00:01:14.715 --> 00:01:15.755
I don't see

00:01:16.395 --> 00:01:18.715
anybody from the public there. So

00:01:19.035 --> 00:01:20.795
I guess the exciting

00:01:20.795 --> 00:01:21.835
questions

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:25.750
on lighting of the athletic fields, that was last

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:29.190
meeting we went through and that will

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:32.950
no interest tonight.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:33.990
But

00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:35.665
at this point,

00:01:36.865 --> 00:01:40.545
Marina, if you can allow me to share my screen, I'll call up the

00:01:41.665 --> 00:01:42.305
other

00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:49.825
regulation changes and we'll work our way through those. And I think they'll be a little quicker than what we had in the past.

00:02:10.675 --> 00:02:11.555
Okay.

00:02:11.555 --> 00:02:15.395
Can everybody see the section five for the ARD?

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:18.850
Yes.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.290
>> Okay, very good.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:21.250
So

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:29.490
Eric asked for a couple of changes on behalf of the town, and I put in a couple of changes just to

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.410
make them consistent

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.445
with what

00:02:34.565 --> 00:02:37.365
we've done a couple of changes in the past. But

00:02:37.685 --> 00:02:40.085
I'm going to go through what's different

00:02:40.325 --> 00:02:42.485
on section five here

00:02:42.565 --> 00:02:43.045
now.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:46.750
And so the first change,

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.590
we talked about

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.630
accessory apartments.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.550
And I added the word subject to affordable housing restrictions

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:56.910
because

00:02:57.915 --> 00:02:59.675
by right, we're going to have

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.515
accessory apartments

00:03:04.075 --> 00:03:05.995
if they're deemed affordable.

00:03:05.995 --> 00:03:07.995
And so I put that in the list here.

00:03:10.235 --> 00:03:12.155
Going down to home occupations,

00:03:12.155 --> 00:03:16.220
I specified as of right, those not requiring a special permit,

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.100
and referred you back to the home occupation section.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.220
And then the change that

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.500
Eric is asking for

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.140
is really a change that's

00:03:29.235 --> 00:03:32.915
provided to us by the state. They say everybody's

00:03:32.915 --> 00:03:34.115
going to go do this.

00:03:34.435 --> 00:03:36.835
And that's to have as of right

00:03:38.915 --> 00:03:40.275
in the

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.770
residential areas

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:47.330
the ability to establish a family day care home

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.610
or a group child care home,

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.290
which is really

00:03:53.825 --> 00:03:56.705
small daycare centers. So I think

00:03:57.105 --> 00:04:01.425
if memory serves me correctly, a family daycare center is six kids

00:04:01.745 --> 00:04:02.865
or fewer,

00:04:03.265 --> 00:04:04.945
and that includes any

00:04:05.105 --> 00:04:06.225
kids that

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:13.190
the daycare center operator has, then the group childcare center goes up to 12.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.390
But the state told us to put

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:18.630
those changes in, and so

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.350
that's why those are here.

00:04:22.445 --> 00:04:23.965
So, at this point,

00:04:25.085 --> 00:04:27.805
I'll ask if there are any questions

00:04:28.205 --> 00:04:32.685
on the changes to as of right in the ARD

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:33.485
area.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.050
Okay.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.050
The next section includes

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:46.650
what we had

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.970
for special permit uses.

00:04:53.305 --> 00:04:54.025
And

00:04:54.585 --> 00:04:56.185
I added the word

00:04:56.825 --> 00:05:00.985
kennels down here. So I thought if anybody was going to put a kennel

00:05:01.385 --> 00:05:03.225
in a residential area,

00:05:03.865 --> 00:05:05.545
we would want that to come

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:12.410
before the Commission and have a public hearing associated with it to get input from the neighbors.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:13.770
So I added

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.970
kennels. If you remember back when we

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:18.970
had the

00:05:19.945 --> 00:05:22.985
discussion on Scott Beebe's kennel application,

00:05:23.865 --> 00:05:26.025
we didn't hold a public hearing

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:29.225
because there's a couple of places where

00:05:29.465 --> 00:05:34.345
it's not clear whether a public hearing was needed or not for Class A kennel.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:41.800
We processed that application because he had a huge field that he was working in. But going forward,

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:50.440
said, I think anybody who is going to be a neighbor to a kennel might want to have a say on that. So I added the word kennel there.

00:05:52.805 --> 00:05:57.525
The other thing we did is I left child care centers in here.

00:05:57.925 --> 00:05:59.925
And again, when we put the definition

00:06:00.245 --> 00:06:04.405
in the definition section, so a child care center for a special permit

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:08.200
is a child care center that has more than 12 kids.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:10.520
So it's larger

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.520
child care center.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:17.400
And we thought if we were going to be more than what the state was telling us, had to allow as of right,

00:06:17.955 --> 00:06:24.355
that would be by special permit. And so I left that in there as opposed to eliminating it where

00:06:24.675 --> 00:06:28.275
that would be the case where we'd only allow the small child care centers.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:33.870
Then at the end here, I added

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:40.830
by special permit accessory apartments not subject to affordable housing restrictions

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:47.835
and also added home occupations requiring a special permit in reference back to the article on

00:06:48.075 --> 00:06:48.795
those.

00:06:49.755 --> 00:06:50.555
So those

00:06:51.275 --> 00:06:52.395
are the changes

00:06:52.955 --> 00:06:54.235
in Section

00:06:54.235 --> 00:06:56.555
five. Any questions on

00:06:56.635 --> 00:06:57.835
the special permit?

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.400
Things.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:11.680
>> Chad, if you have an accessory apartment but you don't want it to fall under affordable housing, you would have to apply through

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.475
a special permit. Right? That's correct. Okay.

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:16.835
>> Yep.

00:07:17.635 --> 00:07:23.315
And I don't know if that means everybody's going to be just doing the special permit or not, but at least we're

00:07:23.315 --> 00:07:24.035
building

00:07:24.675 --> 00:07:25.795
the regulations

00:07:25.795 --> 00:07:36.460
to support affordable housing if we can properly incentivize people to go there. I don't know that we've got that incentive starting out, but our regulations will support it

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:37.980
if and when we get there.

00:07:40.395 --> 00:07:44.475
Okay, I am going to move on to Section 7, which is the Lake District.

00:07:49.755 --> 00:07:51.435
Similar to

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:55.530
what we did in Section 5 back

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:58.970
last January when we were talking about the

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:01.210
municipal buildings,

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:05.770
we put house of worships and cemeteries

00:08:06.065 --> 00:08:08.545
is as of right categories.

00:08:16.465 --> 00:08:19.665
I don't think anybody's going to be building a cemetery in the Lake District

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:22.610
As I'm

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:26.130
thinking about the House of Worship,

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:28.450
I'm trying to

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:32.130
recall.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.290
I think we did change it.

00:08:35.135 --> 00:08:37.695
No, we've got house of worship or cemeteries

00:08:37.855 --> 00:08:39.055
special permit.

00:08:39.135 --> 00:08:39.615
So

00:08:43.935 --> 00:08:47.855
that would be a change. I would like to put the house of worship and a cemetery

00:08:47.855 --> 00:08:48.895
into

00:08:49.375 --> 00:08:50.335
the special

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:55.170
permit category, take it out of there. So that's a mistake on my part.

00:08:56.690 --> 00:08:57.330
If

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:00.130
people feel strongly that it should be there,

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:01.410
we can leave it there.

00:09:02.745 --> 00:09:09.145
It dawned on me that I think we're asking a couple of houses of worship to put in special permits for

00:09:09.465 --> 00:09:10.425
some

00:09:10.665 --> 00:09:12.985
properties that are being used as

00:09:14.185 --> 00:09:15.705
churches and temples.

00:09:16.745 --> 00:09:16.985
So

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:22.080
we should be consistent with that here. So I'll

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.880
take care of that unless somebody on the commission feels strongly that we should be

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:28.720
including that there.

00:09:30.425 --> 00:09:30.985
I

00:09:31.385 --> 00:09:33.145
put in the family daycare

00:09:33.385 --> 00:09:35.545
home, group daycare home,

00:09:35.785 --> 00:09:37.865
just like we did in section five.

00:09:38.905 --> 00:09:39.945
That was based on,

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:46.200
again, the state told us that's what they wanted for residential areas.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.480
I added just to be consistent

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.160
with Section five, and I think it was a good idea

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:58.185
that we list all the as of right things and all the special permit uses.

00:09:58.505 --> 00:10:02.505
So I added home occupations not requiring special permits

00:10:03.625 --> 00:10:07.625
and accessory apartments subject to affordable housing restrictions.

00:10:08.105 --> 00:10:08.985
And also here,

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:11.540
I put C section

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:13.140
4.111

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:15.300
Charlie, which talks about

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:18.820
the minimum lot size in Lake District to have an

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:20.660
accessory apartment

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.500
is, I think, 2.75

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:23.220
acres. So

00:10:25.575 --> 00:10:33.255
that restriction remains in effect even though it's not spelled out right here. If you go back and look in this section, that's what it tells you.

00:10:36.055 --> 00:10:37.655
So

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:41.780
any question on the as of rate uses in the Lake District?

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:48.260
Okay, moving down to the special permit.

00:10:52.375 --> 00:10:57.815
Added municipal land uses similar to what we did in Section five back in January.

00:10:57.895 --> 00:10:59.335
I just didn't want to

00:11:00.455 --> 00:11:08.750
do any more changes than was necessary to get that changed through back then. Added public parks, playgrounds, athletic fields, and beaches,

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:11.790
similar to what we did in Section five.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.590
And added the home occupations requiring special permits

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:20.190
and accessory apartments not subject to affordable housing restrictions.

00:11:21.045 --> 00:11:24.725
Again, I will add the houses of worship and cemeteries

00:11:24.725 --> 00:11:26.965
in the special permit section.

00:11:28.405 --> 00:11:29.045
So

00:11:31.605 --> 00:11:33.845
any questions on the special permit?

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:36.520
Thanks.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:39.560
Okay,

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:43.400
very good. I thought that was kind of straightforward.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:47.720
Next, we're going to talk about Chapter 15 signs.

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:48.840
Again, these

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:50.840
are

00:11:51.845 --> 00:11:53.685
changes that were requested

00:11:53.765 --> 00:11:55.045
by the town.

00:11:56.645 --> 00:11:58.165
The first was a

00:11:58.805 --> 00:12:00.485
change to the definition

00:12:02.485 --> 00:12:04.725
well, not the definition of a billboard, but

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:08.640
right this minute, billboards are

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:10.000
prohibited.

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:14.240
Towns ask that we allow billboards

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:18.960
where specifically authorized by the Board of Selectmen on town owned property.

00:12:21.175 --> 00:12:27.655
I'm

00:12:27.655 --> 00:12:28.615
not completely

00:12:29.015 --> 00:12:29.975
sold on

00:12:30.215 --> 00:12:31.255
this idea

00:12:31.655 --> 00:12:32.135
yet.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.490
My concern goes back to

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:43.050
what we saw during the pandemic with all the signs along the road that

00:12:46.835 --> 00:12:52.115
Sometimes you like signs, sometimes you don't. I'm not sure that the Board of Selectmen

00:12:52.915 --> 00:12:54.595
can specifically

00:12:54.595 --> 00:12:56.275
choose to authorize

00:12:56.675 --> 00:13:00.675
signs. I think when we went through the change that we did most recently,

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:06.390
if somebody wants to put up a sign and you're allowed to put up a sign for one thing,

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:11.750
you have to be able to put up a sign for anything. We are not allowed to regulate the content.

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:14.790
And so that caused me

00:13:15.305 --> 00:13:17.705
a little bit of concern there.

00:13:18.745 --> 00:13:23.865
In addition, I didn't understand exactly how the process was going to work as far as

00:13:24.185 --> 00:13:24.825
when

00:13:25.065 --> 00:13:27.865
somebody wants a sign, who's going to make the sign,

00:13:28.265 --> 00:13:30.345
what's going to standard be, who decides

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:34.640
what kind of sign is appropriate for putting around the park.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:38.960
If the Commission thinks that this is something that we should do,

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:41.280
and I'm going to be

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:42.560
relying

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:46.720
heavily on input from Scott and Ann because

00:13:47.905 --> 00:13:50.305
you two are on the board of Selectman,

00:13:50.305 --> 00:13:51.265
the

00:13:51.265 --> 00:13:53.345
body that was asking for this change.

00:13:53.905 --> 00:13:57.105
We might be able to do something that specifically

00:13:57.105 --> 00:13:57.985
limits

00:13:58.785 --> 00:14:04.170
the signs to the fence around the soccer field or something if that's where it was planned to go.

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:13.290
You know, I don't think we would want to put the regulation in effect that somebody could put a billboard sign up on the

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:16.730
town property on the corner of Lake Road and Route 6, for instance.

00:14:18.445 --> 00:14:24.125
>> Just to clarify, Jed, the signs that we're talking about here were signs

00:14:24.925 --> 00:14:27.965
down at the soccer field along defense

00:14:28.125 --> 00:14:28.445
line,

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:31.400
where the selectmen

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:41.240
thought that it would be good to have, to be able to have the people that are involved with the, the usage of that field to be able to put their, their signs up.

00:14:43.195 --> 00:14:51.915
They were told previously that there was no regulation for them to put their signs up. So we're trying to make it so that they could put their signs up on

00:14:51.995 --> 00:14:54.875
field, on the field fence

00:14:55.275 --> 00:14:55.835
during

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.060
the season.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.180
>> Okay. And and we could we

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:07.500
could restrict the wording on that when we get to deliberation to, you know, further restrict it there.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:12.405
Again, my concern is that if we're selling sign space,

00:15:12.965 --> 00:15:18.165
there might be some folks putting up signs that we're not keen to have posted.

00:15:19.365 --> 00:15:24.325
And I don't know that we could stop them from doing that. I don't know that we could stop the Board of Selectmen from

00:15:24.725 --> 00:15:25.925
not authorizing them.

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:29.750
So we'll

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:30.790
deliberate that.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:34.470
But that was my concern, and I wanted to make sure that was on the record

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:35.910
so that

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:38.150
when we vote

00:15:39.245 --> 00:15:40.925
eventually on the record,

00:15:41.405 --> 00:15:43.885
that concern can be taken into consideration.

00:15:48.765 --> 00:15:49.325
The

00:15:49.805 --> 00:15:51.965
other change that

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:55.420
the town was looking for in

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:00.380
we wanted to add

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:04.700
public interest signs that were erected

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:06.540
as approved by the Board of Selectmen.

00:16:07.065 --> 00:16:10.265
A quantity right now, if you read our

00:16:10.585 --> 00:16:11.465
regulations,

00:16:11.465 --> 00:16:14.985
the quantity would be understood to be one.

00:16:15.705 --> 00:16:20.025
You know, we talked about banners over at the school where there's a significantly

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:23.930
larger quantity. I think that's the right answer. I think

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.090
the Board of Selectmen can

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:27.530
do that

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:32.650
within their purview and not be in any freedom of speech issues or whatever.

00:16:34.745 --> 00:16:35.785
That's that.

00:16:36.985 --> 00:16:37.865
The height,

00:16:39.065 --> 00:16:42.185
again, my sense is that the banners over

00:16:42.505 --> 00:16:45.385
at the school are at an appropriate height.

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:50.210
And right now, that's higher than 12 feet, which I

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:55.010
think our regulation limits it to either 10 feet or 12 feet, something like that.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.130
The town was also asking to increase the size

00:17:01.425 --> 00:17:04.705
from 16 square feet to 32 square feet.

00:17:05.345 --> 00:17:08.145
I think that's reasonable. There was some

00:17:08.625 --> 00:17:09.905
concern that the

00:17:10.785 --> 00:17:11.825
sign that we

00:17:12.465 --> 00:17:15.825
had approved for putting on the senior center

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:18.910
was a little too small at 16 square feet.

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:23.630
I don't know that it needs to be 32 square feet, but that gives

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:27.710
the Board of Selectmen the latitude to go up to that

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:30.190
make that call.

00:17:34.805 --> 00:17:36.725
We got a little feedback from

00:17:37.125 --> 00:17:38.165
our attorney

00:17:42.005 --> 00:17:42.805
on,

00:17:42.805 --> 00:17:45.365
I think, the original words in here

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:46.430
